{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs6Q8o6ctnkdVpoTjATD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A package pinned in the constraints file is no longer subject to `--max-release-age`. `tests/test_cooldown.py` passes (38 tests). Before I moved the test's import into place, I also ran `tests/test_resolver.py` and `tests/test_bootstrap_requirement_resolver.py` alongside it, and all 91 tests passed.\n\n**Fix** (`src/fromager/resolver.py`, in `find_all_matching_from_provider`): when `provider.constraints.get_constraint(req.name)` is set, the age filter is skipped and an info line says so. This covers both modes:\n- **Multi-version mode:** the pinned version is no longer filtered out, so resolution no longer comes back empty.\n- **Single-version mode:** the misleading \"keeping all to avoid empty resolution\" warning is no longer logged for pinned packages.\n\nI also updated the `max_age_cutoff` docstring to say pinned packages are exempt.\n\n**Regression test:** `test_max_release_age_skipped_for_constrained_package` in `tests/test_cooldown.py`. It pins `test-pkg==1.2.2` (84 days old) with a 5-day window. It runs with the fallback both on and off, and in both cases `1.2.2` is returned and the warning is absent.\n\nI couldn't run `ruff`, since `.venv/bin/ruff` doesn't exist. I put the new test import in sorted order by hand. `hatch run lint:fix` and mypy were not run, and I haven't committed anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1385,"cache_read_input_tokens":53061,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1385},"output_tokens":499,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"35ab0abb-4954-4d27-9011-c54de343af52","uuid":"76d40db9-7fe2-46d5-b644-77199